<body>
    <h1>Use Case 2.1.6.5: Admin Assigns Tags for Campaign Categorization fo=
r Creates Campaign Setup (Step-5)</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p><strong>User Story</strong></p>
<p>As an Admin, I want to categorize my phishing simulation campaign using =
tags, so that I can easily organize, search, and filter campaigns based on =
various criteria.</p>
<p><strong>Description</strong></p>
<p>This use case outlines how the Admin assigns tags to a phishing simulati=
on campaign. Tags are used to categorize campaigns, making it easier to sea=
rch, filter, and manage campaigns based on their characteristics. The admin=
 can enter custom tags or select from suggested tags. Tags can be based on =
campaign type, department, target audience, or other relevant factors. This=
 helps in the organization and tracking of campaigns in a structured manner=
.</p>
<p><strong>Actors</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Admin</strong>: Assigns tags to categorize and organize the camp=
aign.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>System</strong>: Displays the tags input section, validates tag =
input, and provides suggested tags.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Preconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin is logged into the campaign creation interface.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The admin is at the <strong>Tags</strong> step in the campaign creation =
process.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Postconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Tags are assigned to the campaign and saved.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The campaign is categorized properly, making it easier to search and fil=
ter based on the assigned tags.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The admin can continue to the next step in the campaign creation process=
.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Main Flow (Normal Success Scenario)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 1: Navigate to Tags Step</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Aspire navigates to the <strong>Tags</strong> step in the <strong>Cr=
eate New Campaign</strong> wizard.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays the <strong>Campaign Tags</strong> interface with an=
 input field for entering tags, along with a list of <strong>Suggested Tags=
</strong>.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 2: Enter Custom Tags</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin clicks in the <strong>Add Tags</strong> input field.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin types the desired tag (e.g., "Phishing", "New Employees") and =
presses <strong>Enter</strong> or the <strong>comma</strong> key to add the=
 tag.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system validates the tag input to ensure it follows the rules (alpha=
numeric characters only, no special characters).</p></li>
<li>
<p>If the tag is valid, it is added to the list of tags for the campaign.</=
p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 3: Select Suggested Tags</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The system displays a list of <strong>Suggested Tags</strong> such as:</=
p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Security</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Awareness</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Phishing</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Training</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>New Employees</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>GDPR</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Compliance</strong></p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can click on any of these <strong>Suggested Tags</strong> to a=
dd them to the campaign=E2=80=99s tags list.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 4: Review Tags</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin can review all the tags added to the campaign.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays the tags in the <strong>Tags</strong> section, confi=
rming that they are properly formatted.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Tags are displayed with a visual check mark and may be removed by clicki=
ng a <strong>delete icon</strong> next to each tag.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 5: Tag Guidelines</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The system provides a guideline for the tags:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Tags must be <strong>alphanumeric</strong> (letters and numbers only).</=
p></li>
<li>
<p>Multiple tags can be separated by commas or <strong>Enter</strong>.</p><=
/li>
<li>
<p>Tags are <strong>case-insensitive</strong>, and duplicates are automatic=
ally removed.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The recommended tagging convention includes department, campaign type, q=
uarter (Q1, Q2, etc.), or risk level.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 6: Save Tags</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>After assigning the tags, the Admin clicks <strong>Save &amp; Continue</=
strong> to save the tags and proceed to the next step in the campaign creat=
ion process.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The tags are now saved and attached to the campaign, and the Admin can m=
ove to the next step in the wizard.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Frontend Form Validation</strong></p>
<p><strong>Field Validation Rules</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Tag Input</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is optional, but at least one tag =
must be added.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Tags must be alphanumeric.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Tags are separated by commas or Enter.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Special characters are not allowed.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Tag must contain only alphanumeric char=
acters. Special characters are not allowed."</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Suggested Tags</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: The Admin can choose tags from the <strong>Su=
ggested Tags</strong> section.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Clicking on any suggested tag automatically adds it to the campaign.</p>=
</li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "No errors for suggested tags."</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Business Rules</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"14=
3c53fa-6d12-45d9-baba-a3ee07abac60" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Rule</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-1</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Tags must be alphanumeric and cannot contain special characters.</p></td=
>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-2</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Tags must be separated by commas or <strong>Enter</strong> key.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-3</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Tags are case-insensitive, and duplicates are automatically removed.</p>=
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-4</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>At least one tag must be assigned to a campaign before it can be saved.<=
/p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-5</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Suggested tags are provided by the system and are meant for easier categ=
orization.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"8a=
39d17d-3fb1-4dcc-8469-848f07ce7ebe" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Pass/Fail Condition</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-01</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can enter custom tags in the <strong>Add Tags</strong> field.</p><=
/td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Tags can be entered and added by pressing <strong>Enter</strong> or <str=
ong>comma</strong>.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-02</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select tags from the <strong>Suggested Tags</strong> list.</p>=
</td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Suggested tags can be selected and added to the campaign tags list.</p><=
/td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-03</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Tags must be alphanumeric and separated by commas or Enter.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Tags are validated, and errors are displayed if invalid characters are u=
sed.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-04</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Add Tags</strong> field allows entering multiple tags, with =
each tag separated by a comma or Enter.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Multiple tags can be added by pressing <strong>Enter</strong> or typing =
a comma.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-05</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The Admin can delete any tag from the list by clicking the <strong>delet=
e</strong> icon next to the tag.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Tags can be removed successfully by clicking the delete icon.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-06</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Tags are displayed correctly below the input field in the <strong>Availa=
ble Tags</strong> list.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Tags appear correctly under the <strong>Available Tags</strong> section.=
</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-07</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Tags are case-insensitive, and duplicates are automatically removed.</p>=
</td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Duplicates are removed, and tags are treated as case-insensitive.</p></t=
d>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-08</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The Admin can proceed to the next step once tags are assigned to the cam=
paign.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> button is enabled after tags ar=
e added.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-09</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can filter tags by category, such as <strong>Security</strong>, <s=
trong>Awareness</strong>, <strong>Phishing</strong>, <strong>GDPR</strong>,=
 etc.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Tags are filtered and displayed correctly based on category.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-10</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can add tags for any type of campaign, including those related to =
<strong>Training</strong> or <strong>Phishing</strong>.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Tags for campaign types are correctly added and displayed.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-11</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system prevents tags with special characters from being added.</p></=
td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Special characters trigger an error message.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-12</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> button is only enabled after at=
 least one valid tag is added.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The button is enabled once a tag is entered or selected.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-13</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin receives an error message if invalid characters (e.g., symbols) ar=
e used in the tag input.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Error message "Invalid characters in tag" is shown.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-14</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The tags are saved successfully and categorized for future reference.</p=
></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Tags are saved and applied to the campaign.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-15</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The Admin can see a list of suggested tags and easily add them to the ca=
mpaign.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Suggested tags are displayed correctly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-16</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Add Tags</strong> field accepts a maximum of 100 characters =
per tag.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Tag length validation is applied to ensure no more than 100 characters.<=
/p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-17</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can filter tags by difficulty level, such as <strong>Easy</strong>=
, <strong>Medium</strong>, <strong>Hard</strong>, etc.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Tags are filtered and categorized by difficulty level.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-18</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Tags are displayed in a clear and organized manner under the <strong>Ava=
ilable Tags</strong> section.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Tags appear clearly in the <strong>Available Tags</strong> section.</p><=
/td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-19</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select multiple tags for categorization (e.g., <strong>New Emp=
loyees</strong>, <strong>High Risk</strong>, etc.).</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Multiple tags can be selected from the list.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-20</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system automatically removes duplicate tags from the list.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Duplicate tags are detected and removed automatically.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>System Behavior &amp; Validation</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Tag Input</strong>: Admin can enter alphanumeric tags, which wil=
l be validated before being added to the campaign.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Tag Suggestions</strong>: Suggested tags are displayed for quick=
 categorization.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Tag Deletion</strong>: Admin can delete any tag by clicking the =
delete icon next to the tag.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Filtering</strong>: Admin can filter tags by category, difficult=
y level, or other criteria.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: The system ensures that only valid tags are=
 accepted.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Security Handling</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Tag Validation</strong>: Tags must adhere to alphanumeric rules =
and cannot include special characters.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Data Privacy</strong>: Tags are stored securely and are accessib=
le only to authorized users.</p></li>
</ul>
    </div>
</body>
